# Enforce LF line endings for every text file, on every platform.
#
# Why this is load-bearing, not cosmetic: several tests assert byte-for-byte
# facts about source files — the Training body's sha256 and line count
# (tests/rendered-html.test.mjs), and structural regexes with literal "\n".
# On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, Git rewrites source to CRLF,
# the "\r" breaks those regexes, and the deploy chain fails at the test gate
# with no real code defect. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working tree identical to
# the repo's stored blobs so the guards hold identically for Windows and Unix.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply text/eol normalization (protects the regenerated
# brand icons and other binaries from corruption).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
